<h2>Segment 220 &mdash; karma without natural existence</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s220S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w1">gnyis pa</span> <span class="u particle" data-d="6" data-l="s220w2">ni</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w3">dngos po</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w4"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220w5">rang bzhin</span> gyis <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220w6">grub pa</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w7">med</span> par <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w8">&#x27;dod pa</span>&#x27;i phyogs la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w9">kun gzhi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w10">sogs</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s220w11">khas ma blangs</span> kyang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w12">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w13">&#x27;bras</span> kyi &#x27;brel pa <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w14">&#x27;thad</span> tshul <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w15">ji ltar</span> yin <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s220w16">zhe na</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s220S">Here is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w1">second point</span> [of still another discussion]. One may <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s220w16">ask</span> the following: Those who <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w8">believe</span> that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w3">entities</span> have <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w7">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w4"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220w5">natural</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220w6">existence</span></span> [meaning the Madhyamika Prasangika (or Consequence) School] do <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s220w11">not accept</span> the concepts of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w9">foundation consciousness</span> and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w10">like</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w15">how</span> then is it that they can still assert that all the workings of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w12">karma</span> and its <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w13">consequences</span> are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w14">totally right and proper</span>?<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s220w2"><span class="nul">Topic particle has no separate English exponent.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first independent proposal. The technical compound rang bzhin gyis grub pa owns natural existence with unique tighter members. Both square-bracketed explanations are supplied and unaligned. 'brel pa is relational; the recast workings of karma does not establish a separate lexical workings equivalent, so it is omitted rather than nulled. phyogs, kyang, tshul and yin are distributed within the English subject/question/concession framing and omitted; no claim assigns the later assert to the earlier khas ma blangs. sogs owns like within the closing gesture, with the supplied and the unwrapped. Question-introduction zhe na is a phrase recast as ask; the English impersonal participant, modal and following-introduction remain unwrapped.</div>
